# Fix Backend Crash (Residual Grades Feature)

The user "cant login" because the backend server is crashing on startup. The crash is caused by a `ModuleNotFoundError` for `models.grade`, which was partially removed in a previous task but residual imports and logic remain in [backend/routers/courses.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/courses.py) and [backend/database.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/database.py).

## Proposed Changes

### Backend

#### [MODIFY] [courses.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/courses.py)
- Remove `from models.grade import GradeComponent, GradeEntry` (Line 15).
- Remove grade calculation logic and data from [get_course](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/courses.py#74-161) (Lines 108-135).
- Remove `grades` and `grade_percentage` from the response in [get_course](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/routers/courses.py#74-161) (Lines 157-158).

#### [MODIFY] [database.py](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/database.py)
- Remove `from models.grade import GradeComponent, GradeEntry` from [init_db](file:///Users/oli/Desktop/CraftCanvas/backend/database.py#15-41) (Line 27) to prevent potential future issues.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run the backend server locally and verify it starts without errors:
  ```bash
  cd backend && source .venv/bin/activate && uvicorn main:app --port 8000
  ```
- Use the `scripts/check_login.py` (to be created/updated) to verify the `/api/v1/auth/status` and `/api/v1/auth/login` endpoints are responsive.

### Manual Verification
- Verify that the login page loads and allows signing in after the backend is stabilized.
- Check the course detail page to ensure it still loads without the grade information.
